    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d219">

                <pb facs="0496" n="400" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg400"/>

                <head>No. 217.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Washburne to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-09-09"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 9, 1873</date>.
                        (Received September 26.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 851.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your dispatch “separate” of
                    July 2, I have the honor to inclose the translation of a dispatch received from
                    the Due de Broglie upon the subject of the coinage of the mint in France,
                    together with a tabular statement of the coinage for the years 1871 and
                    1872.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>E. B. WASHBURNE.</signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d219-a1.xml" xpointer="d219-a1"/>
